theory.intro:
The **displacement** from one position to another is the vector $\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{2})-\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{1})$. It points from the first position to the second. Its magnitude is the distance between the two positions.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-0.6,0)--(6.4,0) node[right,font=\footnotesize] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6)--(0,4.6) node[above,font=\footnotesize] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.6:5.8,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.3*\x*\x-2.0*\x+4.6});
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (1.2,2.632);
\coordinate (Q) at (5.2,2.312);
\draw[->,gray] (O)--(P) node[midway,above left,font=\footnotesize] {$\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{1})$};
\draw[->,gray] (O)--(Q) node[midway,below right,font=\footnotesize] {$\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{2})$};
\draw[->,very thick,red] (P)--(Q) node[midway,above,font=\footnotesize] {$\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{2})-\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{1})$};
\fill (P) circle (2.2pt);
\fill (Q) circle (2.2pt);
\node[below left,font=\footnotesize] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
$\begin{aligned}\underset{\sim}{r}\left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right)&=4\sqrt{3}\,\underset{\sim}{i}+4\underset{\sim}{j}\\\underset{\sim}{r}(\pi)&=-8\underset{\sim}{i}\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned}\underset{\sim}{d}&=\underset{\sim}{r}(\pi)-\underset{\sim}{r}\left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right)\\&=(-8-4\sqrt{3})\underset{\sim}{i}-4\underset{\sim}{j}\end{aligned}$

The distance between the positions is the magnitude of this displacement.

$\begin{aligned}|\underset{\sim}{d}|&=\sqrt{(-8-4\sqrt{3})^{2}+(-4)^{2}}\\&=\sqrt{128+64\sqrt{3}}\\&=8\sqrt{2+\sqrt{3}}\end{aligned}$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.3cm,y=0.3cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{motionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{displacementRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[->,black] (-9,0)--(9,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-9)--(0,9);
\path (9,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,9) node[above] {$y$} (0,0) node[below right] {$O$};
\draw[black] (0,0) circle (8);
\draw[->,motionBlue,thick,domain=30:180,samples=60,variable=\a] plot ({8*cos(\a)},{8*sin(\a)});
\coordinate (A) at ({4*sqrt(3)},4);
\coordinate (B) at (-8,0);
\draw[->,displacementRed,thick] (A)--(B);
\fill[black] (A) circle (2pt);
\fill[black] (B) circle (2pt);
\path (A) node[above right] {$A(4\sqrt{3},4)$} (B) node[above left] {$B(-8,0)$};
\path (-1,2.4) node[above,text=displacementRed] {$\underset{\sim}{d}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The red arrow joins the two positions directly; the blue arc shows the path travelled.

$\begin{aligned}\underset{\sim}{r}(2)&=6\underset{\sim}{i}+8\underset{\sim}{j}\\\underset{\sim}{r}(5)&=15\underset{\sim}{i}-13\underset{\sim}{j}\\\underset{\sim}{d}&=\underset{\sim}{r}(5)-\underset{\sim}{r}(2)\\&=9\underset{\sim}{i}-21\underset{\sim}{j}\end{aligned}$

The displacement points right and down, so it lies in the fourth quadrant.

$\begin{aligned}\alpha&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{21}{9}\right)\\\theta&=360^{\circ}-\alpha\\&\approx293^{\circ}\end{aligned}$

Keep the full precision of $\alpha$ until the final rounding.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{displacementBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (D) at (1.5,-3.5);
\draw[->,black] (-0.5,0)--(2.5,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-4)--(0,0.7);
\path (2.5,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,0.7) node[above] {$y$} (O) node[above left] {$O$};
\draw[->,thick,displacementBlue] (O)--(D);
\draw[dashed,black] (1.5,0)--(D);
\draw[dashed,black] (0,-3.5)--(D);
\path (0.75,0) node[above] {$9$} (0,-1.75) node[left] {$-21$};
\path (D) node[below right,text=displacementBlue] {$\underset{\sim}{d}$};
\draw[black] (0.65,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=-66.8014,radius=0.65];
\path (0.65,-0.4) node[right] {$\alpha$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The vector is translated to the origin to show its direction.

